  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "_doc": "The canonical Brand entity (#246). One entry per brand, keyed by an OPAQUE `id` that is the join key every other file uses (vehicles.json, customer-current-vehicle.json, brand-tiers.json, brand-market-share.json, competitors.json, competitor-archetypes.json) and that the engine persists in saves. `label` is the DISPLAY NAME and is the only brand string a player ever reads — it is a property of the brand, never a key, so relabelling a brand touches this file and nothing else. No vehicle template carries a brand name of its own: the label is resolved from here at construction, so there is exactly one place a brand is named.",
  "_v2Doc": "v1 was a bare record keyed by the brand id with no display name at all, and the name a player saw came from a parallel `make` field on every vehicle template — which is where the real trademarks lived. v2 is the array-of-{id,label,...} idiom data/auction-sources.json already uses. The ids did NOT change, deliberately: they are already opaque join keys (#224), they are persisted inside the inventory / competitorMarket / reputation blobs, and renaming them would be a three-module save migration bought for no player-visible gain.",
